Article 21 If a key emitting entity falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of ecological environment shall order it to make corrections and impose a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; if it refuses to make corrections, it may be ordered to suspend production for rectification:
(1) Failing to formulate and implement a greenhouse gas emission data quality control plan in accordance with the provisions;
(2) Failing to submit emission statistical accounting data and annual emission reports in accordance with the provisions;
(3) Failing to disclose to the public information on emissions, emission facilities, and statistical accounting methods in the annual emission report in accordance with the provisions;
(4) Failing to preserve the original records and management ledgers of the data involved in the annual emission report in accordance with the provisions.

Article 22 If a key emitting entity falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of ecological environment shall order it to make corrections, confiscate the illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than five times but not more than ten times the illegal gains; if there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than 500,000 yuan, a fine of not less than 500,000 yuan but not more than 2 million yuan shall be imposed; a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons; if it refuses to make corrections, its carbon emission allowances for the following year shall be reduced by a proportion of not less than 50% but not more than 100%, and it may be ordered to suspend production for rectification:
(1) Failing to calculate and account for greenhouse gas emissions in accordance with the provisions;
(2) The prepared annual emission report contains major defects or omissions, or data materials are tampered with or forged, false data materials are used, or other fraudulent acts are carried out during the preparation of the annual emission report;
(3) Failing to prepare and submit samples for testing in accordance with the provisions.
